  "_inferred": "Motor Kv and resistance, ESC parameters and airframe drag areas are NOT published. Drag areas come from the entered body and arm geometry, which is where a forward-flight check is most exposed \u2014 unlike hover, cruise power depends on them.",
  "_calibration": "Nothing tuned; usable capacity at the same 80% as the M300 so the two are directly comparable.\n\nValidated at HOVER: 52.1 min. DJI's 55 min is measured at about 8 m/s without payload, and the model gives 64 min at that speed \u2014 more optimistic than its hover figure, because a multirotor at 8 m/s gets translational lift. Which of those DJI's number really refers to is not clear from the datasheet, so the hover comparison is quoted as the conservative one.\n\nAgainst the M300 the sensitivity is right: heavier (6.47 vs 6.3 kg) with less energy (526 vs 548 Wh) gives less endurance (52.1 vs 55.2 min). That direction is the point of having both."
